1
00:00:00,467 --> 00:00:03,500
A candy bar melted
in an engineer's pocket —

2
00:00:03,500 --> 00:00:05,867
and whatever melted
it was invisible.

3
00:00:05,867 --> 00:00:08,067
It was the mid-1940s.

4
00:00:08,067 --> 00:00:11,267
Percy Spencer had been standing
beside a magnetron —

5
00:00:11,267 --> 00:00:14,467
the tube that sends out
radar's invisible waves.

6
00:00:14,467 --> 00:00:16,000
Instead of shrugging it off,

7
00:00:16,000 --> 00:00:17,967
he tested food on purpose.

8
00:00:17,967 --> 00:00:20,667
Popcorn kernels
by the magnetron popped.

9
00:00:20,667 --> 00:00:22,067
An egg exploded.

10
00:00:22,467 --> 00:00:23,667
Then the key step:

11
00:00:23,667 --> 00:00:26,333
he concentrated the waves
in a small space.

12
00:00:26,333 --> 00:00:28,267
Food placed there heated fast.

13
00:00:28,567 --> 00:00:31,100
In October, 1945,

14
00:00:31,100 --> 00:00:34,233
Raytheon filed a patent
for cooking with microwaves.

15
00:00:34,633 --> 00:00:37,167
Microwave ovens
still work that way —

16
00:00:37,167 --> 00:00:40,133
a magnetron filling
a metal box with waves.

17
00:00:40,400 --> 00:00:42,033
Every time you press Start,

18
00:00:42,033 --> 00:00:43,267
you're using the answer

19
00:00:43,267 --> 00:00:45,900
to the question a melted
candy bar raised.
